    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #356\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-236-system-i18n-03-05-load-validate-and-re-thr_gj7akew298` pushed to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #236 ([system-i18n 03/05]): loading, validation, and resolution of module i18n catalogs.\n\n- `ModuleRegistry` now loads an optional `i18n/{cs,en}.json` pair from beside each module's manifest, validating the shape (flat string-to-string map) and enforcing cross-module key uniqueness with the same check-then-commit pattern used for other module identifiers — a module that collides on a catalog key is rejected atomically, with no partial registration.\n- Added a pure `resolveCatalogLabel` resolver implementing the fallback chain from the canonical-keys skill: explicit override → requested locale → English reference catalog → raw canonical key.\n- Shipped a reference `cs`/`en` catalog for the Tasks system database as a working example.\n- `@semprec/data`'s build now copies `i18n/` JSON alongside compiled output.\n- Added unit tests for the resolver, the registry's catalog loading/validation/collision handling, and an end-to-end test against the real Tasks manifest.\n\n## Verification\n- Unit suite: 18 files / 127 tests passed\n- Integration suite: 67 files / 787 tests passed\n- Full build, lint, and dependency-boundary checks passed\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
